# (a) pointer var vs its pointee: FillChar(P^, SizeOf(P)) clears pointer-size bytes (26, 27)
# (b) string element count used as a byte count: missing character-size factor (28, 29, 30)
# (c) FillChar over a managed/reference variable (31 string, 32 TBytes, 33 interface)
# Non-hits: SizeOf(P^) (45), plain record (46), * SizeOf(Char) (47), TBytes element = byte (48),
# * 2 (49), ByteLength (50), plain Integer (51). Fields (66, 67) are silent by design: no visible declaration.
